\v 45 \w The|strong="G2532"\w* \w man|strong="G1519"\w* \w went|strong="G1831"\w* \add and presented himself to the priest. But then\add* \w he|strong="G2532"\w* \w began|strong="G1909"\w* \w to|strong="G1519"\w* tell \w many|strong="G4183"\w* \w people|strong="G1510"\w* \w about|strong="G1909"\w* \add how Jesus had healed him\add* [DOU]. \w As|strong="G1519"\w* \w a|strong="G2532"\w* \w result|strong="G1519"\w*, \w Jesus|strong="G1525"\w* \w was|strong="G1510"\w* \w no|strong="G3371"\w* \w longer|strong="G3371"\w* \w able|strong="G1410"\w* \w to|strong="G1519"\w* \w enter|strong="G1525"\w* \w any|strong="G1909"\w* \w town|strong="G4172"\w* \w publicly|strong="G5320"\w* \add because the crowds would surround him\add*. \w Instead|strong="G1161"\w*, \w he|strong="G2532"\w* \w remained|strong="G1510"\w* \w outside|strong="G1854"\w* \add the towns\add* \w in|strong="G1519"\w* \w places|strong="G5117"\w* \add where no people lived\add*. \w But|strong="G1161"\w* \w people|strong="G1510"\w* \w kept|strong="G2532"\w* \w coming|strong="G2064"\w* \w to|strong="G1519"\w* \w him|strong="G3588"\w* \w from|strong="G2064"\w* \w all|strong="G2532"\w* \w over|strong="G1909"\w* \w that|strong="G3588"\w* region.   
\c 7  
\s1 Some Pharisees and scribes criticized Jesus about his disciples disobeying the traditions of the elders. Jesus replied, showing that their attitudes and practices were mistaken.  
\sr Mark 7:1-23  
\p
\v 1  \add One day some\add* \w Pharisees|strong="G5330"\w* \w and|strong="G2532"\w* \w some|strong="G5100"\w* \w men|strong="G5100"\w* \w who|strong="G3588"\w* \w teach|strong="G5100"\w* \w the|strong="G2532"\w* \add Jewish\add* laws \w gathered|strong="G4863"\w* \w around|strong="G4314"\w* \w Jesus|strong="G2532"\w*. \w They|strong="G2532"\w* \w had|strong="G2532"\w* \w come|strong="G2064"\w* \w from|strong="G2064"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="G2414"\w* \add to investigate him\add*.  
\v 2-4 The Pharisees and all of the \add other\add* Jews \add strictly\add* observe the traditions that their ancestors \add taught. For example, they refuse to\add* eat until they first wash their hands \add with a special ritual\add*, especially after they \add return\add* from \add buying things in\add* the marketplace. \add They think that God will be angry with them if they do not do that, because some person or thing unacceptable to God might have touched\add* ◄\add them/the things they bought\add*►. There are many other such \add traditions\add* that they accept and try to obey. Specifically, they wash \add in a special way\add* their cups, pots, kettles, containers, and beds \add in order that using these things will not make God reject them\add*.   
\p
\v 5 \w That|strong="G3588"\w* \w day|strong="G3588"\w*, \w those|strong="G3588"\w* \w Pharisees|strong="G5330"\w* \w and|strong="G2532"\w* \w men|strong="G4245"\w* \w who|strong="G5101"\w* taught \w the|strong="G2532"\w* \add Jewish\add* laws saw \w that|strong="G3588"\w* \w some|strong="G3588"\w* \w of|strong="G1223"\w* \w his|strong="G1223"\w* \w disciples|strong="G3101"\w* \w were|strong="G3588"\w* \w eating|strong="G2068"\w* food \w with|strong="G1223"\w* \w hands|strong="G5495"\w* \w that|strong="G3588"\w* \w they|strong="G2532"\w* \w had|strong="G2532"\w* \w not|strong="G3756"\w* washed \add using the special ritual\add*. \w So|strong="G2532"\w* \w they|strong="G2532"\w* \w questioned|strong="G1905"\w* \w Jesus|strong="G2532"\w*, saying, “\add Your\add* \w disciples|strong="G3101"\w* disobey \w the|strong="G2532"\w* \w traditions|strong="G3862"\w* \w of|strong="G1223"\w* \w our|strong="G2532"\w* ancestors! ◄\w You|strong="G4771"\w* \w should|strong="G3588"\w* \w not|strong="G3756"\w* \add let them\add* \w eat|strong="G2068"\w* food \w if|strong="G2532"\w* \w they|strong="G2532"\w* \w have|strong="G2532"\w* \w not|strong="G3756"\w* washed \w their|strong="G2532"\w* \w hands|strong="G5495"\w* \add using our special ritual\add*!/\w Why|strong="G5101"\w* \w do|strong="G5101"\w* \w you|strong="G4771"\w* \add let them\add* \w eat|strong="G2068"\w* food \w if|strong="G2532"\w* \w they|strong="G2532"\w* \w have|strong="G2532"\w* \w not|strong="G3756"\w* washed \w their|strong="G2532"\w* \w hands|strong="G5495"\w* \add using our special ritual\add*?► [RHQ]”  
\v 6 \w Jesus|strong="G3004"\w* \w said|strong="G3004"\w* \w to|strong="G3004"\w* \w them|strong="G3588"\w*, “\w Isaiah|strong="G2268"\w* \add rebuked your ancestors\add*, \w and|strong="G1161"\w* \w his|strong="G4012"\w* words describe \w very|strong="G3778"\w* \w well|strong="G2573"\w* \w you|strong="G5210"\w* \w people|strong="G2992"\w* \w who|strong="G3588"\w* only pretend \w to|strong="G3004"\w* \w be|strong="G3588"\w* \w good|strong="G2573"\w*! \w He|strong="G1161"\w* \w wrote|strong="G1125"\w* \w these|strong="G3778"\w* words \add that God said\add*:  
\q1 \w These|strong="G3778"\w* \w people|strong="G2992"\w* \w speak|strong="G3004"\w* \add as if they\add* \w honor|strong="G5091"\w* \w me|strong="G1473"\w*, \w but|strong="G1161"\w* \w they|strong="G1161"\w* [SYN] really \w do|strong="G3004"\w* \w not|strong="G1125"\w* think \w about|strong="G4012"\w* honoring \w me|strong="G1473"\w* \w at|strong="G4012"\w* \w all|strong="G1161"\w*.  
\v 7 \w It|strong="G1161"\w* is useless \w for|strong="G1161"\w* \w them|strong="G1321"\w* \w to|strong="G1161"\w* \w worship|strong="G4576"\w* \w me|strong="G1473"\w*, \w because|strong="G1161"\w* \w they|strong="G1161"\w* \w teach|strong="G1321"\w* only \w what|strong="G1161"\w* people \w have|strong="G1473"\w* commanded \add as if I myself had commanded them\add*.   
\p
\v 8 You, \add like your ancestors\add*, refuse \add to do\add* \w what|strong="G3588"\w* \w God|strong="G2316"\w* \w has|strong="G2316"\w* \w commanded|strong="G1785"\w*. Instead, you follow only \w the|strong="G3588"\w* \w traditions|strong="G3862"\w* \w that|strong="G3588"\w* ◄\w others|strong="G3588"\w*/\w your|strong="G3588"\w* ancestors► \w have|strong="G3588"\w* \add taught\add*.”  
\v 9 \w Jesus|strong="G3004"\w* \w also|strong="G2532"\w* \w said|strong="G3004"\w* \w to|strong="G2443"\w* \w them|strong="G3588"\w*, “\add You think\add* [IRO] \w that|strong="G2443"\w* \w you|strong="G5210"\w* \w are|strong="G3588"\w* clever \w in|strong="G2532"\w* refusing \w to|strong="G2443"\w* \w do|strong="G2532"\w* \w what|strong="G3588"\w* \w God|strong="G2316"\w* \w commanded|strong="G1785"\w* \w just|strong="G2532"\w* \w so|strong="G2443"\w* \w that|strong="G2443"\w* \w you|strong="G5210"\w* \w can|strong="G3004"\w* \w obey|strong="G5083"\w* \w your|strong="G2532"\w* own \w traditions|strong="G3862"\w*!  
\v 10  \add For example, our ancestor\add* \w Moses|strong="G3475"\w* \add wrote God’s\add* \w command|strong="G3004"\w*, ‘\w Honor|strong="G5091"\w* \w your|strong="G5091"\w* \w fathers|strong="G3962"\w* \w and|strong="G2532"\w* \w your|strong="G5091"\w* \w mothers|strong="G3384"\w*’. \w He|strong="G2532"\w* \w also|strong="G2532"\w* wrote, ‘\add The authorities must\add* execute \w a|strong="G2532"\w* person \w who|strong="G3588"\w* \w speaks|strong="G3004"\w* \w evil|strong="G2551"\w* \w about|strong="G3588"\w* \w his|strong="G2532"\w* \w father|strong="G3962"\w* \w or|strong="G2228"\w* \w mother|strong="G3384"\w*.’  
\v 11-12 But you \add teach people that it is all right that people no longer must help their parents. You teach people that it is all right if people\add* give their things to God \add instead of giving them to their parents\add*. You allow them to say to their parents, ‘What I was going to give to you \add to provide for you, I have now promised to\add* give to God. So I \add cannot any longer help you\add*!’ As a result, you are \add actually telling people\add* that they no longer have to help their parents!  
\v 13 \w And|strong="G2532"\w*, \w by|strong="G2532"\w* \w doing|strong="G4160"\w* \w that|strong="G3739"\w*, \w you|strong="G5210"\w* disregard \w what|strong="G3739"\w* \w God|strong="G2316"\w* commanded! \w You|strong="G5210"\w* teach \w your|strong="G2532"\w* own \w traditions|strong="G3862"\w* \w to|strong="G2532"\w* \w others|strong="G3588"\w* \add and tell them strongly that they should obey them\add* \w And|strong="G2532"\w* \w you|strong="G5210"\w* \w do|strong="G4160"\w* \w many|strong="G4183"\w* \w other|strong="G4183"\w* \w things|strong="G3588"\w* \w like|strong="G5108"\w* \w that|strong="G3739"\w*.”   
\p
\v 14 \w Then|strong="G2532"\w* \w Jesus|strong="G3004"\w* \w again|strong="G3825"\w* \w summoned|strong="G4341"\w* \w the|strong="G2532"\w* \w crowd|strong="G3793"\w* \add to come closer. Then\add* \w he|strong="G2532"\w* \w said|strong="G3004"\w* \w to|strong="G2532"\w* \w them|strong="G3588"\w* \add figuratively\add*, “\w All|strong="G3956"\w* \w of|strong="G2532"\w* \w you|strong="G3004"\w* \w people|strong="G3793"\w* listen \w to|strong="G2532"\w* \w me|strong="G1473"\w*! \add Try to\add* \w understand|strong="G4920"\w* [DOU] \add what I am about to tell you\add*.  
\v 15-16 Nothing that people eat causes \add God to\add* consider them to be unacceptable. On the contrary, it is that which comes from people’s ◄inner beings/hearts► that causes God to reject them.”   
